Subject: [PATCH] toolkit: GNOME search provider owns the org.aequera.browser identity

Why Firefox source must change:
  The GNOME shell search provider's bus name and object path are baked into
  browser/components/shell as org.mozilla.* templates. No build option,
  branding directory, or preference redirects them. Left as-is, an Aequera
  Linux build that enables the provider owns
  org.mozilla.aequera.SearchProvider, violating docs/RESTRICTIONS.md (no
  org.mozilla.* service is claimed).

What it changes (1 file):
  - browser/components/shell/nsGNOMEShellDBusHelper.cpp: bus and object-path
    templates become the fixed desktop identity org.aequera.browser
    (.SearchProvider / /org/aequera/browser/SearchProvider), and the two
    getters return them directly instead of formatting the app-derived leaf.
    Unlike the main app bus (0001, app-derived so channels and
    MOZ_DBUS_APP_NAME keep working), the provider is paired 1:1 with the
    shipped desktop entry, so it shares the desktop entry's identity.
    Matches the shipped
    aequera/design/branding/linux/org.aequera.browser.search-provider.ini
    and .SearchProvider.service, which name exactly this bus.

Depends on: 0001 (same series; independent hunks, applies alone too).
Validation: aequera patch check (applies cleanly); Linux build + run under
  GNOME: provider bus visible, search-provider .ini BusName/ObjectPath match
  the owned names.
Upstream risk: low. Defines plus two getters in stable desktop-integration
  code.

diff --git a/browser/components/shell/nsGNOMEShellDBusHelper.cpp b/browser/components/shell/nsGNOMEShellDBusHelper.cpp
index 2c3157fffdc2..e1e3165ee7ed 100644
--- a/browser/components/shell/nsGNOMEShellDBusHelper.cpp
+++ b/browser/components/shell/nsGNOMEShellDBusHelper.cpp
@@ -13,27 +13,19 @@
 #include "nsImportModule.h"
 #include "nsIOpenTabsProvider.h"
 
-#define DBUS_BUS_NAME_TEMPLATE "org.mozilla.%s.SearchProvider"
-#define DBUS_OBJECT_PATH_TEMPLATE "/org/mozilla/%s/SearchProvider"
+// Aequera: the GNOME search provider is paired with the shipped desktop
+// entry (org.aequera.browser.desktop), so it carries the fixed desktop
+// identity, not the app-derived bus leaf. Matches
+// aequera/design/branding/linux/org.aequera.browser.search-provider.ini.
+#define DBUS_BUS_NAME_TEMPLATE "org.aequera.browser.SearchProvider"
+#define DBUS_OBJECT_PATH_TEMPLATE "/org/aequera/browser/SearchProvider"
 
 const char* GetDBusBusName() {
-  static const char* name = []() {
-    nsAutoCString appName;
-    gAppData->GetDBusAppName(appName);
-    return ToNewCString(nsPrintfCString(DBUS_BUS_NAME_TEMPLATE,
-                                        appName.get()));  // Intentionally leak
-  }();
-  return name;
+  return DBUS_BUS_NAME_TEMPLATE;
 }
 
 const char* GetDBusObjectPath() {
-  static const char* path = []() {
-    nsAutoCString appName;
-    gAppData->GetDBusAppName(appName);
-    return ToNewCString(nsPrintfCString(DBUS_OBJECT_PATH_TEMPLATE,
-                                        appName.get()));  // Intentionally leak
-  }();
-  return path;
+  return DBUS_OBJECT_PATH_TEMPLATE;
 }
 
 static bool GetGnomeSearchTitle(const char* aSearchedTerm,
